- for each weight pair, compute ensemble OOF accuracy after threshold tuning
- keep the best pair
This is still easy to implement and usually better than equal averaging.

A practical final recipe:
- Model A = original 5-fold CatBoost pipeline
- Model B = feature-engineered CatBoost variant
- collect OOF/test probabilities from both
- do weighted average
- tune one final threshold on the blended OOF
- create submission from the blended test probabilities

This keeps both solutions mostly intact, avoids risky refactoring, and gives the strongest low-complexity ensemble.
